; Every ASN scalar in one vector, including the two Core §2 already produces for
; other purposes: `()` is unit, and `_` is nil in a position the language grammar
; has no phrase for. Neither costs a new lexeme, which is the whole basis of the
; claim that ASN shares the language's lexical structure rather than forking it.
;
; canonical: [1 -1 1.5 -1.5 "text" "he said \"hi\"" true false () :status _]

[1 -1 1.5 -1.5 "text" "he said \"hi\"" true false () :status _]
